@fklabach thanks for the issue.

> `set_disconnected()` just doesn't reset _target_uuid_initialized, keep the uuid of the prevously connected device (an obtained uuid never changes in my application, this might not work for others).

Could you make a pull request for this suggestion? I'd say this makes more sense.

How about maintaining Remote client info as part of class `UdpConnection` ?
```cpp
class UdpConnection : Connection  {
    ....
    struct RemoteClient {
        uint8_t sysid = 0;
        uint8_t compid = 0;
        std::string ip = {};
        int port = 0;
    };
    std::vector<RemoteClient> _remote_clients = {};
};
```
instead of:
```cpp
class UdpConnection : Connection  {
    ....
    std::string _remote_ip = {};
    int _remote_port_number = 0;
};

```
We then would send messages only on that remote ip/port of that component.
We can keep  one connection per System rather than per component; then we could have one instance of `UdpConnection::RemoteClient` per component of a System. Sounds fine ?

